message: "If you use this benchmark or its published results, please cite it."
title: "The Startrise LLM Benchmark: frontier models on real single-shot frontend builds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Petrov
    given-names: Misha
    affiliation: Startrise LLC
  - name: Startrise AI Labs
repository-code: "https://github.com/startriseio/sr-llm-benchmark"
url: "https://www.startrise.io/benchmark/"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
keywords:
  - llm-benchmark
  - frontend
  - llm-as-a-judge
  - evaluation
  - webgl
  - accessibility
abstract: >
  A benchmark in which frontier language models each build the same twelve
  single-shot frontend deliverables (Three.js, WebGL, landing page, 3D game,
  accessible interface, brownfield change request, SVG icon system, stateful
  application, zero-JavaScript page, HTML email, and two open briefs). Every
  deliverable is driven in headed Chromium, scored blind by a three-lab judge
  panel on four axes with median aggregation, and rated blind by a human. The
  repository contains the harness, the briefs, the configuration, and the
  published per-run results.
